--- accepted-reader-protocol-v16-template.txt
+++ proposed-reader-protocol-v17-template.txt
@@ -16,6 +16,8 @@
 
 Independently recompute every numerical case result and every volunteered remaining quantity from the question's stated starting state and the attached rule. Use arithmetic code when useful; verify starting quantities, each change, any cap or rounding rule, and the final quantity. When describing a sequence, replay its operations in order and cross-check every stated ordinal or intermediate state against the remaining and final quantities; all descriptions must agree with the same calculation. A correct general quotation does not excuse a wrong numerical statement. Check each separately named permission, prohibition or alternative against the complete relevant source unit; give a distinct ruling for each requested alternative rather than assuming a ruling about one action answers a question about another. Do not invent a prohibition merely from an ordering instruction. Remove unnecessary numerical claims instead of introducing extra guesses; retain every actually asked concrete result. This review is a generic method, not another rules source.
 
+Before saving the final output, compare each complete answer with the exact literal question, rather than only your requested_parts paraphrase. For every asked case, state the resulting condition or quantity, including any remainder; a conditional rule or exchange formula alone is not a resolved case. Read yes/no openings as answers to the literal question and ensure all following prose agrees. Distinguish a quantity for each object from the combined total; recompute both and check every stated intermediate amount. Repair any disagreement in your own complete entry, then check the final wording again. Apply this to every question without using facts beyond the two authorized inputs.
+
 For each question, explicitly enumerate its own clauses in requested_parts. Select complete appropriate operative units from the summary and attach them WITHIN THAT SAME answer entry: a whole blank-line-bounded paragraph, a complete list item including any continuation lines, a complete heading-bounded subsection, or the full relevant table including its headers. Keep every relevant condition and outcome within the selected unit; do not stop a quote just before a later condition. A broad procedure request can require multiple adjacent units or the complete procedure subsection. Select all relevant operative steps for that request, rather than stopping at the first paragraph containing a keyword. If different clauses concern separate procedures, attach the relevant complete units for each. For each evidence unit record unit_type (paragraph, list_item, table, or subsection), zero-based Unicode start/end offsets and the exact text. Exclude only leading/trailing whitespace from a complete unit; preserve all internal text and newlines. A table unit must include its headers. These offsets must select complete units from the frozen summary. Quote each selected unit once within an entry, without duplicating it under several labels. Avoid unrelated whole-summary dumps. Add only the minimal case conclusion and actual arithmetic the question asks. Check EACH of your own requested clauses against its attached operative text; every clause must be answered or explicitly unsupported. Same-entry complete operative quotations count as part of the answer. State actual calculated values when asked, not just formulas or generic support labels. Do not borrow support from another question, and ensure your case prose agrees with your quotes.
 
 SOURCE BOUNDARIES BEFORE SAVING: Construct quotations programmatically from actual newline, paragraph/list and heading boundaries in the supplied summary; never select a fixed excerpt character length. For tables, select complete rows from the beginning of a line through its final pipe, preserving the relevant local column header and separator row and any controlling introduction or legend. Quoting the whole relevant table is acceptable; attach a complete controlling intro/legend as a separate complete unit when outside the table. Use full blank-line paragraph boundaries or complete list-item boundaries with all continuation lines for prose. During your own original review, mechanically check each selected span and exact text against these boundaries before saving each batch/final output; repair accidental midword/midrow cuts at that stage. Check the relevant header and controlling prose are included in this SAME entry. This check is rule-agnostic; do not read another file or use external hints. Optional source-boundary diagnostics are format notes, not substantive grades. Correct requested facts supplied anywhere in the same complete entry count; a technical crop alone does not make an otherwise complete correct ruling factually wrong. Material omissions or contradictions still matter.
